spec gg02-detach-delete-hub-vs-edge-create-lpg: 2 sessions, 6 permutations
# GG02. s1 DETACH DELETEs a hub with three incoming edges; s2 creates x->hub. One
# is refused in every order: no edge into the dead hub survives, and the relationship
# count agrees with the arcs the probe walks.
# Through the lpg API: detach-delete hub; AddEdge(x, hub).
# The final dangling probe must count 0 in every permutation: an edge to a dead node
# is never committed (catalogue §9 point 3).

starting permutation: s1d s1c s2e s2c
step s1d: lpg: detach-delete hub (RemoveEdge of each in-arc, RemoveAllEdgesFrom, RemoveNode)
step s1c: lpg: Session.EndVersionedTx
step s2e: lpg: AddEdge(x, hub)
ERROR: serialization conflict
step s2c: lpg: Session.EndVersionedTx
ERROR: serialization conflict
final rels: MATCH ()-[r:R]->() RETURN count(r) AS rels
rels
----
0   
